Dear Xiaobo,

Thank you for pointing this out; the link should hopefully be repaired shortly.  In addition to Ken Scheve's MI program, another manner to combine quantities of interest across imputed datasets from Amelia, within Stata, is the "mi estimate:" command.  There is a short explanation of this command, and how to most easily take imputed datasets from Amelia into the stacked format that Stata uses using Stata's "mi import" at the end of section 4.9, page 44 of the current Amelia manual.  This may perhaps be of additional use.

http://r.iq.harvard.edu/docs/amelia/amelia.pdf

James 

